# Margin environment variables. Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) if you want to
# keep values around; nothing reads a .env file automatically yet, so export
# them in your shell. Never commit real secrets.
#
# --- Desktop (Electron main process) — all optional ---------------------------
# Library folder holding your .md files (default: ~/Documents/Margin)
# MARGIN_LIBRARY_DIR=/path/to/folder
# Electron userData folder (default: OS default; tests use a temp folder)
# MARGIN_USER_DATA_DIR=/path/to/folder
# Load this URL instead of the static export (set automatically by `pnpm dev:desktop`)
# MARGIN_DEV_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:8081
# Expo web export folder (default: packaged Resources/web or apps/app/dist)
# MARGIN_WEB_DIR=/path/to/apps/app/dist
# Show the window without taking OS keyboard focus (automated tests)
# MARGIN_SHOW_INACTIVE=1
# Simulate a filesystem without hard links, e.g. exFAT (tests)
# MARGIN_TEST_NO_HARDLINKS=1
# Cap the library listing (default 50000) to test the truncation notice
# MARGIN_TEST_LIST_LIMIT=3
#
# Margin server origin for Sign In… (default http://127.0.0.1:3000, the local dev
# server). Can also be set as "serverUrl" in userData/settings.json.
# MARGIN_SERVER_URL=https://margin.example.com
#
# --- Server (apps/server) ------------------------------------------------------
# Production values live in Vercel environment variables ONLY. For local dev, put
# them in apps/server/.env.local (git-ignored; read by `pnpm dev:server`).
# Owner setup (GitHub OAuth App, ids, revoking): docs/server-setup.md.
#
# This server's own origin. Must equal the OAuth App's callback host.
# PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# From the GitHub OAuth App for this environment.
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Who may sign in: comma-separated login:numericId pairs (both must match).
# Find your id: curl -s https://api.github.com/users/<login> | grep '"id"'
# ALLOWED_GITHUB_LOGINS=lyonsv:1234567
# >= 32 random chars (openssl rand -base64 48); seals the short-lived sign-in cookie.
# AUTH_SECRET=
# Storage: Vercel injects BLOB_STORE_ID (+ VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN) when a private Blob
# store is connected. BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN only to use a real store locally.
# BLOB_STORE_ID=
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
# Local dev only (refused on Vercel): keep tokens in memory.
# MARGIN_STORE=memory
# Local dev server port (default 3000).
# PORT=3000
# Tests only: point the server at a mock GitHub. Leave unset.
# GITHUB_OAUTH_URL=
# GITHUB_API_URL=
